From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 07:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: hci_bcm: Add BCM4375 support

The BCM4375B1 of the Galaxy S10+ speaks the same protocol as the chips this
driver already drives, so the entry carries no quirks: the two that exist
here were each added after someone measured the chip that needed them, and
nobody has measured this one yet.

Read from the vendor device tree of the Galaxy S10+ (SM-G975F): the
controller sits on the PERIC1 serial port, with the enable line on gpm8-0
and the two wake lines on gpg2-0 and gpa2-3.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
index 1a4fc3882fd..0f925a6fc20 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
@@ -1590,6 +1590,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id bcm_bluetooth_of_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "brcm,bcm43430a1-bt" },
 	{ .compatible = "brcm,bcm43438-bt", .data = &bcm43438_device_data },
 	{ .compatible = "brcm,bcm4349-bt", .data = &bcm43438_device_data },
+	{ .compatible = "brcm,bcm4375-bt" },
 	{ .compatible = "brcm,bcm43540-bt", .data = &bcm4354_device_data },
 	{ .compatible = "brcm,bcm4335a0" },
 	{ .compatible = "cypress,cyw4373a0-bt", .data = &cyw4373a0_device_data },
